{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":84182,"duration_api_ms":84143,"num_turns":20,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"9286c758-3a8f-4642-bae4-1af4ab2d33c5","total_cost_usd":0.44160175,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32755,"cache_read_input_tokens":285576,"output_tokens":3762,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":32755,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":9,"outputTokens":3762,"cacheReadInputTokens":285576,"cacheCreationInputTokens":32755,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.44160175,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Verified each amendment against the current codebase state. The duplicate-function/compile-break amendments (b7d3b861 and 3f8f27ee) do not match the current code — only single definitions exist. The denitrification test confounder (757b2d8b) has already been fixed. The Ca/Mg defensive guard (b9bf2e92) is a real robustness issue — both update_molt_stress and molt_mineral_modifier divide by ca_min_mg_per_l and mg_min_mg_per_l without .max(0.01) guards, while gh_min_d already has one. The HighDensity variant (4bfedb7f) is indeed dead code but is not a correctness/safety issue. The snapshot dominant_repro_suppression drift (4af528d5) is a real diagnostic accuracy issue — it omits the molt-stress factor and merges TAN/nitrite into a single \"chemistry\" bucket rather than tracking them separately.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-2-b7d3b861","decision":"reject","rationale":"Verified the current codebase: density_repro_factor, tan_repro_factor, and no2_repro_factor each have exactly one definition (lines 1458, 1476, 1487). dominant_repro_suppression is defined at snapshot.rs:375. The described compile error does not exist in the current branch."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-757b2d8b","decision":"reject","rationale":"The test_denitrification_reduces_nitrate_accumulation test uses long_horizon_denitrification_state, which now sets nutrient_store_mg_n_total to 0.0 for both the active and control cases (lines 96 and 111). The confounder described in this amendment has already been fixed."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-b9bf2e92","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed: gh_min_d uses .max(0.01) at line 451 and line 1548, but ca_min_mg_per_l and mg_min_mg_per_l have no such guard. In update_molt_stress (lines 459, 464), division by zero params produce NaN/Inf. In molt_mineral_modifier (lines 1557-1558), division by zero ca_min_mg_per_l or mg_min_mg_per_l similarly produces non-finite values that propagate through clamp. This is an asymmetry with the GH guard that should be fixed for consistency and robustness."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-4bfedb7f","decision":"reject","rationale":"HighDensity is confirmed as dead code (only declared at events.rs:49, never referenced elsewhere in src/). However, this is a benign unused enum variant — not a correctness, safety, or robustness defect. It may represent planned future functionality for density-dependent reproduction events. Removing it is cleanup, not a necessary fix."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-3f8f27ee","decision":"reject","rationale":"This is a duplicate of fr-2-b7d3b861 describing the same alleged compile errors. Verified: no duplicate function definitions exist, snapshot.rs defines dominant_repro_suppression locally at line 375 without any conflicting import. The code compiles successfully."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-4af528d5","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified the divergence: update_reproductive_readiness (line 670) uses 7 factors including f_molt (molt stress, line 679) and separate f_tan/f_no2 factors (lines 681-682). The snapshot's dominant_repro_suppression (line 375) omits molt stress entirely, merges TAN and nitrite into a single 'chemistry' bucket (lines 398-413), and only reports 5 factors (line 415). This means the snapshot diagnostic can identify 'chemistry' as the dominant suppressor when the real model would say 'tan' vs 'nitrite', and it cannot surface molt stress as a dominant factor at all. This discrepancy will mislead debugging and telemetry."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"9a9f75ca-dc71-4577-a727-ca978e898185"}
